---
import LegalDoc from "../components/LegalDoc.astro";
import InfoLayout from "../layouts/InfoLayout.astro";

const sections = [
    ["agreement", "This agreement"],
    ["eligibility", "Eligibility"],
    ["accounts", "Your account"],
    ["addresses", "Addresses"],
    ["content", "Your content"],
    ["acceptable-use", "Acceptable use"],
    ["moderation", "Moderation and takedown"],
    ["reports", "Reports and copyright"],
    ["plans", "Free service and paid plans"],
    ["ours", "Tondo's own materials"],
    ["help", "Help me"],
    ["third-parties", "Third-party links and services"],
    ["disclaimers", "Disclaimers"],
    ["liability", "Limit of liability"],
    ["indemnity", "Indemnity"],
    ["ending", "Ending and deletion"],
    ["changes", "Changes"],
    ["law", "Governing law and disputes"],
    ["general", "General terms"],
    ["contact", "Contact"],
] as const;
---

<InfoLayout
    title="Terms of service"
    description="The agreement between you and GalleoApp, Inc. for using Tondo, including its rules for pages and addresses."
>
    <LegalDoc effective="November 1, 2026" sections={sections}>
        <h2 id="agreement">This agreement</h2>
        <p>
            These terms are an agreement between you and GalleoApp, Inc., a Delaware corporation
            that operates Tondo at tondo.page ("we" or "us"). They apply when you create an account,
            publish a page or otherwise use Tondo. By doing any of those, you agree to them. Please
            read them with our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, which explains how we handle
            personal information.
        </p>
        <p>
            Tondo lets you claim an address and publish a page of links and other content there.
            It's in early development, so features can change and some things shown on the site
            aren't available yet.
        </p>

        <h2 id="eligibility">Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
            You must be at least 18 and legally able to enter this agreement. If you use Tondo for
            an organization, you confirm that you have authority to bind it, and "you" includes that
            organization. You can't use Tondo if we've previously removed you from it, or if the law
            bars you from using it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="accounts">Your account</h2>
        <p>
            Give an email address you control, and keep your password and sign-in method secure. You
            are responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us at{" "}
            <a href="mailto:legal@tondo.page">legal@tondo.page</a> if you think someone else has got
            into it. We may contact you at your account email about the service, your account or
            these terms.
        </p>

        <h2 id="addresses">Addresses</h2>
        <p>
            Your address is the part after tondo.page/, such as tondo.page/maya. Choosing one gives
            you permission to use it while your account is in good standing, and doesn't give you
            ownership of it or any other right in it.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Reserved addresses.</strong> Some addresses can't be claimed, including
                words our site uses or could use, such as login, support and privacy, words that
                could pass for Tondo, and addresses used by our example pages. We can add to this
                list.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Changing or giving one up.</strong> If you change your address or delete
                your account, the old address stops working and someone else can claim it straight
                away. We don't redirect old addresses, and we can't control what a later owner does
                with one.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Taking one back.</strong> We may remove, reassign or hold an address if it
                infringes a trademark or other right, impersonates someone or misleads people,
                breaks these terms, or is needed to meet a legal duty. We may also reclaim one that
                appears inactive, such as one with no live page for a long period. We don't do this
                automatically today, and we'll try to contact you at your account email first unless
                the matter is urgent or the law prevents it.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Addresses of removed pages.</strong> An address taken down for abuse stays
                out of use, including after the account is deleted.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="content">Your content</h2>
        <p>
            You keep ownership of the text, photos, links and other material you add to Tondo.
            You're responsible for it, and you confirm that you have the rights and permissions
            needed to use it there, including from anyone pictured or named.
        </p>
        <p>
            You give us a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, store, copy,
            convert, resize, display and distribute your content as needed to run, secure and
            improve Tondo and show your page to anyone who visits it. Our service providers can use
            this licence on our behalf. It lets us do what the service needs, and doesn't let us
            sell your content.
        </p>
        <p>
            The licence ends when you remove the content or delete your account, except for copies
            in backups until they expire, copies we must keep by law, and records of abuse
            decisions. We can't remove copies that others have made of a public page, such as search
            engine results. A published page is public, so don't put anything on it that you need to
            keep private.
        </p>

        <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
            You agree not to use Tondo to do any of the following, or to help anyone else do them:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Phish, or collect passwords, payment details or other sensitive information through
                deception, including by linking to a page that does.
            </li>
            <li>
                Impersonate a person, company or organization, or suggest a connection with one that
                you don't have. Commentary and parody are fine if they're clearly labelled as such.
            </li>
            <li>Commit or promote fraud, scams or deceptive offers.</li>
            <li>
                Link to or spread malware, or disguise where a link goes, including through chains
                of redirects meant to avoid our checks.
            </li>
            <li>
                Share material that sexualizes or exploits minors, or sexual images of anyone
                without their consent.
            </li>
            <li>
                Threaten, harass or incite violence or hatred against people, or publish someone's
                private information without their permission.
            </li>
            <li>Infringe copyright, trademark, privacy or other rights.</li>
            <li>Sell or promote anything illegal, or otherwise break the law.</li>
            <li>Send spam, or use a page mainly as a destination for unsolicited messages.</li>
            <li>
                Interfere with Tondo, probe it for weaknesses without our permission, get around its
                limits or suspensions, inflate view or click counts, or reach it by automated means
                that place an unreasonable load on it.
            </li>
            <li>
                Claim addresses in bulk, or in order to resell them or hold them from their rightful
                users.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="moderation">Moderation and takedown</h2>
        <p>
            We don't review every page before it goes live, and we don't promise to find every
            breach. We can check pages and links, act on reports, and refuse links to destinations
            on a blocklist we keep. A blocked link can't be published, and one that's blocked later
            stops working.
        </p>
        <p>
            If we reasonably believe that a page, link or account breaks these terms, puts people at
            risk or creates legal risk, we may remove content, block links, take a page down, or
            suspend or close the account. A page that's taken down stops being shown at its address
            and can't be published again, and its address can't be changed. You can still sign in
            and delete your account.
        </p>
        <p>
            We'll generally tell you what we did and why, unless doing so would create a risk, get
            in the way of an investigation or break the law. We may act first and explain
            afterwards. If you think we made a mistake, email{" "}
            <a href="mailto:legal@tondo.page">legal@tondo.page</a> and we'll review it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="reports">Reports and copyright</h2>
        <p>
            To report a page that impersonates someone, deceives people or shares harmful material,
            use the "Report this page" link at the bottom of the page, or email{" "}
            <a href="mailto:report@tondo.page">report@tondo.page</a> with the page's address and
            what's wrong with it. We can't promise a particular outcome or response time. Please
            only send reports you believe are accurate and in good faith.
        </p>
        <p>
            To complain about copyright infringement, email{" "}
            <a href="mailto:legal@tondo.page">legal@tondo.page</a> with the following:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>your name, contact details and your signature, which can be typed</li>
            <li>the work you say is infringed</li>
            <li>the address of the page and where the material appears on it</li>
            <li>a statement that you believe in good faith that the use isn't authorized</li>
            <li>
                a statement that your notice is accurate and, under penalty of perjury, that you're
                the rights holder or are authorized to act for them
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            We may remove the material and send your notice to the page's owner. If your material
            was removed and you believe that was a mistake, you can reply with your contact details,
            the material concerned and a statement of why it should be restored, including that you
            accept the jurisdiction of the appropriate court where the law requires it. We may close
            the accounts of repeat infringers. A false notice can make you liable for damages.
        </p>

        <h2 id="plans">Free service and paid plans</h2>
        <p>
            Tondo is free to use right now, and we don't take payment for it. Free use can come with
            limits, such as how many photos you can store, and we can change them.
        </p>
        <p>
            We may offer paid plans in future. Plans and prices shown on the site today are
            placeholders, and you can't buy them. Before you're ever charged, we'll show you the
            price and billing terms and ask you to agree to them. We can also decide that a feature
            needs a paid plan. If that affects something you already use, we'll tell you in advance.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ours">Tondo's own materials</h2>
        <p>
            The Tondo software, name, logo, looks, artwork and site content belong to us or our
            licensors. You may use the looks and artwork as part of your Tondo page while using the
            service. These terms give you no other right to copy or use them. If you send us
            feedback, we may use it without owing you anything.
        </p>

        <h2 id="help">Help me</h2>
        <p>
            Help me is an AI assistant that can change your draft when you ask it to. Its answers
            and changes can be wrong, so check names, prices, dates and anything else that matters
            before you rely on them. It can't publish your page. Publishing is your decision, and
            you're responsible for what you publish, including text and images it made.
        </p>
        <p>
            Don't ask it to read a site that isn't yours or that you don't have the right to use. We
            don't promise that a generated image or logo is free of other people's rights, and we
            can't check it against existing trademarks. Credits for Help me are limited, can change,
            and aren't money. Unused credits don't carry over.
        </p>

        <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party links and services</h2>
        <p>
            Tondo pages link to sites and services we don't run, and we don't endorse or answer for
            them. If you follow a link, that site's own terms and privacy policy apply. Tondo also
            relies on services from other companies, such as Google sign-in, Google Fonts and
            Google's Gemini API, and we can't guarantee their availability.
        </p>

        <h2 id="disclaimers">Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
            We provide Tondo "as is" and "as available". To the extent the law allows, we disclaim
            all warranties, whether express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a
            particular purpose, title and non-infringement. We don't promise that Tondo will always
            be available or free of errors, or that it will keep your content safe from every loss,
            so keep your own copy of anything important. Content on pages belongs to the people who
            published it, and we don't check that it's accurate.
        </p>

        <h2 id="liability">Limit of liability</h2>
        <p>
            To the extent the law allows, neither you nor we are liable under these terms for
            indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive losses, or for lost profits,
            revenue, data or goodwill. Our total liability arising out of Tondo or these terms is
            limited to the greater of the fees you paid us for Tondo in the 12 months before the
            event that gave rise to the claim, or US$100.
        </p>
        <p>
            These limits don't apply to fraud, or to any liability the law doesn't allow us to
            exclude or limit. Your rights as a consumer that can't be waived aren't affected.
        </p>

        <h2 id="indemnity">Indemnity</h2>
        <p>
            If someone makes a claim against us because of your content, your page or your breach of
            these terms, you agree to cover our reasonable losses and costs from that claim,
            including legal fees. We'll tell you about the claim where we can. This doesn't apply to
            the extent the claim was caused by our own breach, or where the law where you live
            doesn't allow it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ending">Ending and deletion</h2>
        <p>
            You can stop at any time. Unpublishing takes your page offline and keeps your account.
            Deleting your account from the Account page removes your page, your photos, your numbers
            and your address, and it can't be undone. The{" "}
            <a href="/privacy#retention">privacy policy</a> explains what can remain, including in
            backups.
        </p>
        <p>
            We may suspend or end your access if you break these terms, if the law requires it, or
            to protect people or the service. We may also change or stop Tondo or any part of it. If
            we're closing the service, we'll give you reasonable notice where we can, so you can
            save what you need. Sections that by their nature should continue, including your
            responsibility for your content, disclaimers, liability, indemnity and governing law,
            continue after this agreement ends.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
        <p>
            We may update these terms as Tondo changes. We'll post the new version here with a new
            effective date. If a change is material, we'll also tell you by email or in the product
            before it takes effect. If you continue using Tondo after that, the new terms apply. If
            you don't agree, you can delete your account before they take effect.
        </p>

        <h2 id="law">Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
            Delaware law governs these terms, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules, and
            disputes are subject to the competent state and federal courts in Delaware. Mandatory
            consumer protections and any right to bring a claim in a local court that can't lawfully
            be excluded aren't affected. These terms don't require arbitration or waive class-action
            rights.
        </p>

        <h2 id="general">General terms</h2>
        <p>
            These terms and our privacy policy are the whole agreement between us about Tondo. If
            part of them can't be enforced, the rest still applies. If we don't enforce something
            straight away, we can still enforce it later. You can't transfer this agreement without
            our consent. We can transfer it as part of a merger, sale or reorganization.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Send questions and legal notices to GalleoApp, Inc. at{" "}
            <a href="mailto:legal@tondo.page">legal@tondo.page</a>. For privacy requests, email{" "}
            <a href="mailto:privacy@tondo.page">privacy@tondo.page</a>. To report a page, email{" "}
            <a href="mailto:report@tondo.page">report@tondo.page</a>.
        </p>
    </LegalDoc>
</InfoLayout>
